By Wikipedia contributors. Each is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Changes: each is an excerpt (the introduction and part of the history
section), as plain text without references, images or tables. The excerpts
are shared under the same licence.


=== Papers and research, English (papers/en/) ===

Three papers from arXiv, each under CC BY 4.0, as shown on the paper's arXiv
page (https://arxiv.org/abs/<number>, "license"). Full papers.

- "Self-RAG (Asai et al., 2023).pdf": Akari Asai, Zeqiu Wu, Yizhong Wang,
  Avirup Sil and Hannaneh Hajishirzi, "Self-RAG: Learning to Retrieve,
  Generate, and Critique through Self-Reflection", arXiv:2310.11511 (2023).
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11511 . CC BY 4.0.
- "Fine-Tuning or Retrieval (Ovadia et al., 2023).pdf": Oded Ovadia,
  Menachem Brief, Moshik Mishaeli and Oren Elisha, "Fine-Tuning or Retrieval?
  Comparing Knowledge Injection in LLMs", arXiv:2312.05934 (2023).
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.05934 . CC BY 4.0.
- "Ragas (Es et al., 2023).pdf": Shahul Es, Jithin James, Luis Espinosa-Anke
  and Steven Schockaert, "Ragas: Automated Evaluation of Retrieval Augmented
  Generation", arXiv:2309.15217 (2023). https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.15217 .
  CC BY 4.0.


