=== Reports and analysis, English (reports/en/) ===

Executive summaries of three World Bank regional economic updates of April
2026, each under CC BY 3.0 IGO, as stated on the World Bank Open Knowledge
Repository page and in the report ("This work is available under the Creative
Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO license"). Original work by The World Bank. These
are excerpts: this is an adaptation of an original work by The World Bank.
Views and opinions expressed in the adaptation are the sole responsibility of
the author or authors of the adaptation and are not endorsed by The World
Bank. Third-party material that the reports credit to others is not covered
by this licence. The World Bank's name and logo are not licensed; the covers
(which carry the logo) are left out.

- "Africa Economic Update, April 2026 (executive summary).pdf": World Bank,
  "Africa Economic Update, April 2026: Making Industrial Policy Work in
  Africa". https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44533 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2333-6 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary (pages 2 to 10 of the published executive-summary file; its cover
  is left out).
- "Latin America and the Caribbean Economic Update, April 2026 (executive
  summary).pdf": William Maloney, Guillermo Vuletin and Andres Zambrano,
  "Revisiting Industrial Policy: Strategic Options for Today", Latin America
  and the Caribbean Economic Update (April 2026), World Bank.
  https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44606 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2337-4 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary (pages xi to xviii of the report).
- "South Asia Economic Update, April 2026 (executive summary).pdf": World
  Bank, "South Asia Economic Update, April 2026: Working with Industrial
  Policy". https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44482 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2326-8 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary file as published by the World Bank.


